message: "If you use EnaGIS, please cite it as below."
title: "EnaGIS: evidence-labelled screening of agricultural storage sites for productive-use energy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mugisha
    given-names: Elie
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Elie1Z/EnaGIS"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
keywords:
  - productive use of energy
  - agriculture
  - GIS
  - grain storage
  - reproducibility
  - OSEAS
abstract: >-
  EnaGIS ranks documented agricultural aggregation points for productive-use-energy
  investigation, with an evidence label on every value and UNKNOWN never defaulted.
  Pilot: Alberta and Saskatchewan primary grain elevators (AAFC 2024). It includes a
  preregistered spatial siting experiment (verdict KILL) and a shipping-point hindcast.
  Energy values come from a temporary, unapproved scenario. Field verification n = 0.
